source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A delimiter a backslash precedes is no candidate at all, so the scan passes it and closes on the last asterisk; Jira bolds the escaped asterisk and the literal one, and jiro reads the same bold effect.
-- input.jira --
*a\*b*c*
-- rendered.html --
<p><b>a&#42;b*c</b></p>
-- want.md --
**a\*b\*c**
-- warnings.json --
[]
